\end{equation}

It follows from the Feynman-Kac formula that $u(t,x) = \E{\varphi(X^x_t)}$ \cite{oksendal2003stochastic}. Replacing $\varphi$ by a neural network ${\widehat{\varphi}}^\varepsilon$ with $\norm{\varphi-{\widehat{\varphi}}^\varepsilon}_{C^0} \leq  \varepsilon$ gives us for any probability measure $\mu$ that,
\begin{equation}\label{eq:kolmogorov1}
