Using \cite[Lemma A.2]{deryck2021pinn} (which is based on \cite{grohs2018proof}) we find, 
\begin{equation}
    \E{(I)} := \E{\left(\int_{D}\abs{\E{{\widehat{\varphi}}^\varepsilon(X^x_t)}-\frac{1}{m}\sum_{i=1}^m {\widehat{\varphi}}^\varepsilon(X^x_t(\omega_m))}^2\mu(dx)\right)^{1/2}} \leq \frac{2\norm{{\widehat{\varphi}}^\varepsilon}_{C^0}}{\sqrt{m}}.
