with notation and random variables cf. Definition \ref{def:MLP}. Note that for every $t\in[0,T]$, $n\in\mathbb{N}$, $\theta\in\Theta$, every realization of the random variable $\widehat{U}_n^\theta(t,\cdot)$ is a neural network that maps from $\mathbb{T}^d$ to $\mathbb{R}$. 

Let $n\in\mathbb{N}_0$, $m\in\mathbb{N}$ and $t\in [0,T]$ be arbitrary. 








Integrating the square of the error bound of Theorem \ref{thm:mlp} and Fubini's theorem tell us that
\begin{equation}\label{eq:fubini}
\begin{split}
   \E{\int_{\mathbb{T}^d}\abs{U^0_n(t,x)-u(t,x)}^2d\mu(x)} &= \int_{\mathbb{T}^d} \E{\abs{U^0_n(t,x)-u(t,x)}^2} d\mu(x)\\
   &\leq \frac{4\mathcal{L}^2 (T+1)^2\exp(2LT)(1+2LT)^{2n}}{m^{n}\exp(-m)}. 
